# 4. TEXT

_publ_section_synopsis
.
_publ_section_abstract
;
A novel microporous strontosilicate material AES-19 was successfully
synthesized by employing a mechanochemical method in which a precursor was
prepared by the solid-state mechanochemical reaction of parent materials and
crystallized by the hydrothermal treatment in an aqueous alkaline medium. The
crystal structure analysis demonstrated that this material was composed of a
unique silicate layer having a two-dimensional eight-membered ring (8MR)
micropore system interconnected through 6-coordinated strontium atoms. This
structure reminds a hypothetical synthesis route to obtain a novel three
dimensional 8MR zeolite via extraction of connecting strontium atoms and
subsequent topotactic condensation of silicate layers.
;

_publ_section_comment
;
(type here to add)
;

_publ_section_exptl_prep      # Details of the preparation of the sample(s)
                              # should be given here.
;
Bruker D8-Advance with V\ario1 diffractometer operated at 40 kV and 50 mA
equipped with a Ge(111) monochromator and a linear position-sensitive
V\%ANTEC-1 detector (8\% 2<i>q</i>) in a modified Debye--Scherrer geometry
using Cu K\a~1~ radiation. Samples were sealed into borosilicate capillary
tubes with an inner diameter of 0.5 mm.
;

_publ_section_exptl_refinement
